  "Question": "The points in a scatter plot generally extend from the lower left to the upper right. What does this indicate?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Negative correlation",
    "B": "It must be the functional relationship \\(y=x\\)",
    "C": "Positive correlation",
    "D": "No correlation"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "When \\(x\\) increases, \\(y\\) generally increases as well. This is called positive correlation. The points do not lie on the same straight line, so this is not a deterministic function.",
